      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T15:58:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I interpreted the existing `context.okay` approach has being a kind of \"--keep-going\", to collect several errors before failing. If we\u0027re going to fail fast, why not just do away with `context.okay` and use `panic` ?",
      "revId": "4b37af5faca1c818cebff3e5e89c970766c6acc1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f749c6ec_34bce886",
        "filename": "bp2build/symlink_forest.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 252,
      "author": {
        "id": 1903985
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T16:09:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "well I am not totally against that this is a more graceful handling of error and worth keeping.",
      "parentUuid": "18ec8dc7_1d8d942b",
      "revId": "4b37af5faca1c818cebff3e5e89c970766c6acc1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ccbb6f8a_79c7e091",
        "filename": "bp2build/symlink_forest.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 252,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T16:13:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that context.okay with fail-fast adds complexity with no added benefit (I don\u0027t think it is more graceful). We want the program to failfast and exit in the event of an error, now, which is expressly what panic is for.",
      "parentUuid": "f749c6ec_34bce886",
      "revId": "4b37af5faca1c818cebff3e5e89c970766c6acc1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c2f05be_80a287ad",
        "filename": "bp2build/symlink_forest.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 252,
      "author": {
        "id": 1903985
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T16:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Graceful in a few ways:\n1. There won\u0027t multiple stack traces in the event of an error\n2. Instead of a worker go-routine panicking, it lets the parent context determine what it wants to do (e.g. any clean-up or logging for instance)\n3. Were one to add unit tests for this (as one should), not using panic would probably be more test-friendly.",
      "parentUuid": "ccbb6f8a_79c7e091",
      "revId": "4b37af5faca1c818cebff3e5e89c970766c6acc1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7213cd68_02d2b838",
        "filename": "bp2build/symlink_forest.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 252,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T16:34:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Multiple stack traces seems like a feature. Also, even with context.okay, we may see multiple error messages for concurrent threads (because multiple threads may have already checked context.okay here, and then failed later)\n2. Do we need this? (YAGNI?)\n3. with Helper, you can unit test with panic() just fine, no?",
      "parentUuid": "3c2f05be_80a287ad",
      "revId": "4b37af5faca1c818cebff3e5e89c970766c6acc1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
